# Quick Start Guide

**Get n8n running in under 5 minutes!**

Choose your Linux distribution and follow the commands below.

---

## Arch-based Linux (Garuda, Manjaro, EndeavourOS)

### One-Command Installation

```bash
bash <(curl -sL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/YOUR_USERNAME/n8n-local-setup/main/install-arch.sh)
```

### Manual Installation (Copy & Paste)

```bash
# Install Docker
sudo pacman -Syu
sudo pacman -S docker docker-compose
sudo systemctl start docker
sudo systemctl enable docker
sudo usermod -aG docker $USER
newgrp docker

# Create n8n directory
mkdir -p ~/.n8n && cd ~/.n8n

# Create configuration
cat > docker-compose.yml << 'EOF'
version: '3.8'
services:
  n8n:
    image: n8nio/n8n:latest
    container_name: n8n
    restart: unless-stopped
    ports:
      - "5678:5678"
    environment:
      - N8N_BASIC_AUTH_ACTIVE=true
      - N8N_BASIC_AUTH_USER=admin
      - N8N_BASIC_AUTH_PASSWORD=changeme123
      - GENERIC_TIMEZONE=Asia/Kolkata
    volumes:
      - ~/.n8n:/home/node/.n8n
EOF

# Start n8n
docker-compose up -d
```

**Access:** http://localhost:5678  
**Login:** admin / changeme123

